</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Petersburg,_Alaska" title="Petersburg, Alaska">Petersburg</a></td>
<td>Home Rule</td>
<td>2013</td>
<td>Incorporated after voters approved borough formation in December 2012.</td>
<td>Named for Norwegian immigrant Peter Buschmann (1849-1903), founder of the former city of Petersburg.</td>
<td>1.18
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003343600000000000♠">3,436</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003290100000000000♠">2,901</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003751400000000000♠">7,514</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Alaska_highlighting_Petersburg_Census_Area.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Petersburg Borough"><img alt="State map highlighting Petersburg Borough" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Map_of_Alaska_highlighting_Petersburg_Census_Area.svg/250px-Map_of_Alaska_highlighting_Petersburg_Census_Area.svg.png" decoding="async" width="150" height="79" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Map_of_Alaska_highlighting_Petersburg_Census_Area.svg/330px-Map_of_Alaska_highlighting_Petersburg_Census_Area.svg.png 2x" data-file-width="1470" data-file-height="777" /></a></span>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/Sitka,_Alaska" title="Sitka, Alaska">Sitka</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/02220,00">220</a>
