</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/St._Johns,_Arizona" title="St. Johns, Arizona">St. Johns</a></td>
<td>1879</td>
<td>Yavapai County</td>
<td>The <a href="/wiki/Apache" title="Apache">Apache</a> (<i>Ndee</i>) people. <i>Apache</i> is an <a href="/wiki/Exonym" class="mw-redirect" title="Exonym">exonym</a> from <a href="/wiki/Zuni_language" title="Zuni language">Zuni</a> <i>ʔapaču</i> "<a href="/wiki/Navajo_people" class="mw-redirect" title="Navajo people">Navajos</a>" or <a href="/wiki/Yavapai_language" title="Yavapai language">Yavapai</a> <i>ʔpačə</i> "enemy".
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004648000000000000♠">64,800</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004112180000000000♠">11,218</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7004290540000000000♠">29,054</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Arizona_highlighting_Apache_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Apache County"><img alt="State map highlighting Apache County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Map_of_Arizona_highlighting_Apache_County.svg/120px-Map_of_Arizona_highlighting_Apache_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="100" height="123" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Map_of_Arizona_highlighting_Apache_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Arizona_highlighting_Apache_County.svg.png 1.5x" data-file-width="893" data-file-height="1099" /></a></span>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/Cochise_County,_Arizona" title="Cochise County, Arizona">Cochise&#32;County</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/04003,00">003</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Bisbee,_Arizona" title="Bisbee, Arizona">Bisbee</a></td>
<td>1881</td>
<td>Pima County</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Cochise" title="Cochise">Cochise</a> (1805-1874), a <a href="/wiki/Chiricahua" title="Chiricahua">Chiricahua</a> <a href="/wiki/Apache" title="Apache">Apache</a> chief and leader of an 1861 uprising. <i>Cochise</i> is an <a href="/wiki/Anglicisation" title="Anglicisation">anglicisation</a> of <i>K'uu-ch'ish</i> "oak".
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7005125773000000000♠">125,773</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003621900000000000♠">6,219</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7004161070000000000♠">16,107</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
