<td>1852</td>
<td>Mariposa</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Tulare_Lake" title="Tulare Lake">Tulare Lake</a>, which is named after the tule rush (<i><a href="/wiki/Schoenoplectus_acutus" title="Schoenoplectus acutus">Schoenoplectus acutus</a></i>) that grew in the marshes and sloughs along its shores</td>
<td>General Law
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7005483546000000000♠">483,546</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003482400000000000♠">4,824</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7004124940000000000♠">12,494</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_California_highlighting_Tulare_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Tulare County"><img alt="State map highlighting Tulare County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Map_of_California_highlighting_Tulare_County.svg/120px-Map_of_California_highlighting_Tulare_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="100" height="115" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Map_of_California_highlighting_Tulare_County.svg/250px-Map_of_California_highlighting_Tulare_County.svg.png 1.5x" data-file-width="916" data-file-height="1054" /></a></span>
<p><br />
</p>
