</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Sonora,_California" title="Sonora, California">Sonora</a></td>
<td>1850</td>
<td><i><b>original</b></i></td>
<td>Exact etymology disputed; probably a corruption of the native term <i>talmalamne,</i> which means "cluster of stone wigwams", a reference to local cave dwelling tribes</td>
<td>General Law
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004538930000000000♠">53,893</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003223600000000000♠">2,236</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003579100000000000♠">5,791</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_California_highlighting_Tuolumne_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Tuolumne County"><img alt="State map highlighting Tuolumne County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Map_of_California_highlighting_Tuolumne_County.svg/120px-Map_of_California_highlighting_Tuolumne_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="100" height="115" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Map_of_California_highlighting_Tuolumne_County.svg/250px-Map_of_California_highlighting_Tuolumne_County.svg.png 1.5x" data-file-width="916" data-file-height="1054" /></a></span>
<p><br />
