</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Marysville,_California" title="Marysville, California">Marysville</a></td>
<td>1850</td>
<td><i><b>original</b></i></td>
<td>Named either by the <a href="/wiki/Maidu" title="Maidu">Maidu</a> people, a local Native American tribe who live on the banks of the <a href="/wiki/Feather_River" title="Feather River">Feather</a> and <a href="/wiki/Yuba_River" title="Yuba River">Yuba Rivers</a>, for one of their villages, or by <a href="/wiki/Gabriel_Moraga" title="Gabriel Moraga">Gabriel Moraga</a> for the wild grapes (<i><a href="/wiki/Vitis_californica" title="Vitis californica">Vitis californica</a></i>) that grow abundantly at the edge of the rivers (<i>uva</i> being Spanish for "grape")</td>
<td>General Law
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004874690000000000♠">87,469</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7002630000000000000♠">630</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003163200000000000♠">1,632</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_California_highlighting_Yuba_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Yuba County"><img alt="State map highlighting Yuba County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Map_of_California_highlighting_Yuba_County.svg/120px-Map_of_California_highlighting_Yuba_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="100" height="115" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Map_of_California_highlighting_Yuba_County.svg/250px-Map_of_California_highlighting_Yuba_County.svg.png 1.5x" data-file-width="916" data-file-height="1054" /></a></span>
