<td><a href="/wiki/Brighton,_Colorado" title="Brighton, Colorado">Brighton</a></td>
<td><span data-sort-value="000000001902-11-15-0000" style="white-space:nowrap">Nov 15, 1902</span></td>
<td>Split from <a href="/wiki/Arapahoe_County,_Colorado" title="Arapahoe County, Colorado">Arapahoe County</a>.</td>
<td>Named in honor of <a href="/wiki/Alva_Adams_(governor)" title="Alva Adams (governor)">Alva Adams</a>, the 5th, 10th, and 14th <a href="/wiki/Governor_of_Colorado" title="Governor of Colorado">Governor</a> of the State of Colorado.
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7005542973000000000♠">542,973</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003118229000000000♠">1,182.29</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003306200000000000♠">3,062</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Adams_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Adams County"><img alt="State map highlighting Adams County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Adams_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Adams_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="150" height="109" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Adams_County.svg/330px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Adams_County.svg.png 2x" data-file-width="1558" data-file-height="1128" /></a></span>
<p><br />
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/Alamosa_County,_Colorado" title="Alamosa County, Colorado">Alamosa&#32;County</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/08003,00">003</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Alamosa,_Colorado" title="Alamosa, Colorado">Alamosa</a></td>
<td><span data-sort-value="000000001913-03-08-0000" style="white-space:nowrap">Mar 8, 1913</span></td>
<td>Split from <a href="/wiki/Costilla_County,_Colorado" title="Costilla County, Colorado">Costilla County</a> and <a href="/wiki/Conejos_County,_Colorado" title="Conejos County, Colorado">Conejos County</a>.</td>
<td>Named for the <a href="/wiki/Populus_sect._Aegiros" class="mw-redirect" title="Populus sect. Aegiros">cottonwood trees</a> which grow along the <a href="/wiki/Rio_Grande" title="Rio Grande">Rio Grande</a> and its tributaries.  <i>Alamosa</i> is a Spanish word for a <i>cottonwood grove</i>.
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004166890000000000♠">16,689</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7002723210000000000♠">723.21</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003187300000000000♠">1,873</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Alamosa_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Alamosa County"><img alt="State map highlighting Alamosa County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Alamosa_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Alamosa_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="150" height="109" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Alamosa_County.svg/330px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Alamosa_County.svg.png 2x" data-file-width="1558" data-file-height="1128" /></a></span>
<p><br />
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/Arapahoe_County,_Colorado" title="Arapahoe County, Colorado">Arapahoe&#32;County</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/08005,00">005</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Littleton,_Colorado" title="Littleton, Colorado">Littleton</a></td>
<td><span data-sort-value="000000001861-11-01-0000" style="white-space:nowrap">Nov 1, 1861</span></td>
<td>Created as one of the 17 original counties of the <a href="/wiki/Territory_of_Colorado" class="mw-redirect" title="Territory of Colorado">Territory of Colorado</a>.  Renamed South Arapahoe County for the five months from November 15, 1902 to April 11, 1903.</td>
<td>Named for predecessor <a href="/wiki/Arapahoe_County,_Kansas_Territory" title="Arapahoe County, Kansas Territory">Arapahoe County, Kansas Territory</a>, which in turn was named for the <a href="/wiki/Arapaho_Nation" class="mw-redirect" title="Arapaho Nation">Arapaho Nation</a> of <a href="/wiki/Native_American_(U.S.)" class="mw-redirect" title="Native American (U.S.)">Native Americans</a>.
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7005666918000000000♠">666,918</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7002804410000000000♠">804.41</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003208300000000000♠">2,083</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Arapahoe_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Arapahoe County"><img alt="State map highlighting Arapahoe County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Arapahoe_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Arapahoe_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="150" height="109" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Arapahoe_County.svg/330px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Arapahoe_County.svg.png 2x" data-file-width="1558" data-file-height="1128" /></a></span>
<p><br />
</p>
</td></tr>
