</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Las_Animas,_Colorado" title="Las Animas, Colorado">Las Animas</a></td>
<td><span data-sort-value="000000001870-02-11-0000" style="white-space:nowrap">Feb 11, 1870</span></td>
<td>Split from <a href="/wiki/Huerfano_County,_Colorado" title="Huerfano County, Colorado">Huerfano County</a> and former Cheyenne and Arapaho tribal land.</td>
<td>Named in honor of frontier trader <a href="/wiki/William_Bent" title="William Bent">William Bent</a>.
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003577900000000000♠">5,779</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003154107000000000♠">1,541.07</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003399100000000000♠">3,991</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Bent_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Bent County"><img alt="State map highlighting Bent County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Bent_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Bent_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="150" height="109" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Bent_County.svg/330px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Bent_County.svg.png 2x" data-file-width="1558" data-file-height="1128" /></a></span>
<p><br />
