</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Boulder,_Colorado" title="Boulder, Colorado">Boulder</a></td>
<td><span data-sort-value="000000001861-11-01-0000" style="white-space:nowrap">Nov 1, 1861</span></td>
<td>Created as one of the 17 original counties of the <a href="/wiki/Territory_of_Colorado" class="mw-redirect" title="Territory of Colorado">Territory of Colorado</a>.</td>
<td>Named for the abundance of <a href="/wiki/Granite" title="Granite">granite</a> <a href="/wiki/Boulder" title="Boulder">boulders</a> along <a href="/wiki/Boulder_Creek_(Colorado)" title="Boulder Creek (Colorado)">Boulder Creek</a>.
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7005330262000000000♠">330,262</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7002740480000000000♠">740.48</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003191800000000000♠">1,918</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Boulder_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Boulder County"><img alt="State map highlighting Boulder County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Boulder_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Boulder_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="150" height="109" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Boulder_County.svg/330px-Map_of_Colorado_highlighting_Boulder_County.svg.png 2x" data-file-width="1558" data-file-height="1128" /></a></span>
<p><br />
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/City_and_County_of_Broomfield,_Colorado" class="mw-redirect" title="City and County of Broomfield, Colorado">City and County of Broomfield</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/08014,00">014</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Broomfield,_Colorado" title="Broomfield, Colorado">Broomfield</a></td>
<td><span data-sort-value="000000002001-11-15-0000" style="white-space:nowrap">Nov 15, 2001</span></td>
<td>Split from <a href="/wiki/Boulder_County,_Colorado" title="Boulder County, Colorado">Boulder</a>, <a href="/wiki/Adams_County,_Colorado" title="Adams County, Colorado">Adams</a>, <a href="/wiki/Jefferson_County,_Colorado" title="Jefferson County, Colorado">Jefferson</a>, and <a href="/wiki/Weld_County,_Colorado" title="Weld County, Colorado">Weld</a> counties and reorganized as a <a href="/wiki/Consolidated_city-county" title="Consolidated city-county">consolidated city and county</a>.</td>
<td>Named for the <a href="/wiki/Broom_corn" class="mw-redirect" title="Broom corn">broom corn</a> that was formerly grown in the area.
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004783230000000000♠">78,323</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7001335700000000000♠">33.57</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7001870000000000000♠">87</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
