<td><span data-sort-value="000000001861-11-01-0000" style="white-space:nowrap">Nov 1, 1861</span></td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Guadalupe_County,_Colorado_Territory" class="mw-redirect" title="Guadalupe County, Colorado Territory">Guadalupe County</a>, one of the 17 original counties of the <a href="/wiki/Territory_of_Colorado" class="mw-redirect" title="Territory of Colorado">Territory of Colorado</a>, was renamed <a href="/wiki/Conejos_County,_Colorado" title="Conejos County, Colorado">Conejos County</a> after six days on November 7, 1861.</td>
<td>Named for the <a href="/wiki/Cottontail_rabbit" title="Cottontail rabbit">cottontail rabbits</a> in the area.  <i>Conejos</i> is a Spanish word for <i>rabbits</i>.
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003754900000000000♠">7,549</span>
