<p><br />
</p>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/Montrose_County,_Colorado" title="Montrose County, Colorado">Montrose&#32;County</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/08085,00">085</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Montrose,_Colorado" title="Montrose, Colorado">Montrose</a></td>
<td><span data-sort-value="000000001883-02-11-0000" style="white-space:nowrap">Feb 11, 1883</span></td>
<td>Split from <a href="/wiki/Gunnison_County,_Colorado" title="Gunnison County, Colorado">Gunnison County</a>.</td>
<td>Named for the town of <a href="/wiki/Montrose,_Colorado" title="Montrose, Colorado">Montrose</a>, which in turn was probably named from the novel <i><a href="/wiki/A_Legend_of_Montrose" title="A Legend of Montrose">A Legend of Montrose</a></i>, published in 1819 by <a href="/wiki/Walter_Scott" title="Walter Scott">Walter Scott</a>.
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004448060000000000♠">44,806</span>
</td>
