</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Worcester,_Massachusetts" title="Worcester, Massachusetts">Worcester</a></td>
<td>1731</td>
<td>From parts of Hampshire County, Middlesex County and Suffolk County. Government abolished in 1998.<sup id="cite_ref-sec-state_4-8" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-sec-state-4"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>4<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup></td>
<td>For its county seat of <a href="/wiki/Worcester,_Massachusetts" title="Worcester, Massachusetts">Worcester</a>, which is named in honor of the <a href="/wiki/England" title="England">English</a> city of <a href="/wiki/Worcester,_England" title="Worcester, England">Worcester</a> and the English Civil War <a href="/wiki/Battle_of_Worcester" title="Battle of Worcester">Battle of Worcester</a> in 1651, a <a href="/wiki/Parliament_of_England" title="Parliament of England">Parliamentarian</a> victory
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7005881248000000000♠">881,248</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003151300000000000♠">1,513</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003391900000000000♠">3,919</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
