<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/San_Juan_County,_Utah" title="San Juan County, Utah">San Juan&#32;County</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/49037,00">037</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Monticello,_Utah" title="Monticello, Utah">Monticello</a></td>
<td><span data-sort-value="000000001880-02-17-0000" style="white-space:nowrap">Feb 17, 1880</span></td>
<td>Parts of <a href="/wiki/Kane_County,_Utah" title="Kane County, Utah">Kane</a>, <a href="/wiki/Iron_County,_Utah" title="Iron County, Utah">Iron</a>, and <a href="/wiki/Piute_County,_Utah" title="Piute County, Utah">Piute</a> counties</td>
<td>Named for the <a href="/wiki/San_Juan_River_(Colorado_River)" class="mw-redirect" title="San Juan River (Colorado River)">San Juan River</a>, a 400-mile (640&#160;km) tributary of the Colorado river located in southern <a href="/wiki/Colorado" title="Colorado">Colorado</a> and Utah<sup id="cite_ref-38" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-38"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>38<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004146010000000000♠">14,601</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7003782000000000000♠">7,820</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7004202540000000000♠">20,254</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Utah_highlighting_San_Juan_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting San Juan County"><img alt="State map highlighting San Juan County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Map_of_Utah_highlighting_San_Juan_County.svg/120px-Map_of_Utah_highlighting_San_Juan_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="100" height="125" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Map_of_Utah_highlighting_San_Juan_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Utah_highlighting_San_Juan_County.svg.png 1.5x" data-file-width="891" data-file-height="1113" /></a></span>
<p><br />
</p>
