VIRGINIA
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/Accomack_County,_Virginia" title="Accomack County, Virginia">Accomack&#32;County</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/51001,00">001</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Accomac,_Virginia" title="Accomac, Virginia">Accomac</a></td>
<td>1663</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Accomac_Shire" title="Accomac Shire">Accomac Shire</a> was established in 1634 as one of the original eight <a href="/wiki/Shires_of_Virginia" title="Shires of Virginia">shires of Virginia</a>. In 1642, it was renamed Northampton County. Then in 1663, Northampton County was divided into two counties. The southern half remained Northampton County while the northern half became Accomac County -- later renamed Accomack with a "k."</td>
<td>From the Native American word Accawmack, meaning "on the other side", referencing the county's position across <a href="/wiki/Chesapeake_Bay" title="Chesapeake Bay">Chesapeake Bay</a>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004334110000000000♠">33,411</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7002455000000000000♠">455</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003117800000000000♠">1,178</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Accomack_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Accomack County"><img alt="State map highlighting Accomack County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Accomack_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Accomack_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="150" height="65" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Accomack_County.svg/330px-Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Accomack_County.svg.png 2x" data-file-width="2495" data-file-height="1082" /></a></span>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/Albemarle_County,_Virginia" title="Albemarle County, Virginia">Albemarle&#32;County</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/51003,00">003</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Charlottesville,_Virginia" title="Charlottesville, Virginia">Charlottesville</a></td>
<td>1744</td>
<td>In 1744, the <a href="/wiki/Virginia_General_Assembly" title="Virginia General Assembly">Virginia General Assembly</a> created Albemarle County by taking the northern portion of <a href="/wiki/Goochland_County,_Virginia" title="Goochland County, Virginia">Goochland County</a>.</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Willem_Anne_van_Keppel,_2nd_Earl_of_Albemarle" class="mw-redirect" title="Willem Anne van Keppel, 2nd Earl of Albemarle">Willem Anne van Keppel, 2nd Earl of Albemarle</a>, colonial proprietary governor
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7005117313000000000♠">117,313</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7002723000000000000♠">723</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7003187300000000000♠">1,873</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Albemarle_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Albemarle County"><img alt="State map highlighting Albemarle County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Albemarle_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Albemarle_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="150" height="65" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Albemarle_County.svg/330px-Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Albemarle_County.svg.png 2x" data-file-width="2495" data-file-height="1082" /></a></span>
</td></tr>
<tr>
