<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/Northampton_County,_Virginia" title="Northampton County, Virginia">Northampton&#32;County</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/51131,00">131</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Eastville,_Virginia" title="Eastville, Virginia">Eastville</a></td>
<td>1634</td>
<td>Original county of the Colony under England, initially named <a href="/wiki/Accomac_Shire" title="Accomac Shire">Accomac Shire</a>. In 1642, it was renamed Northampton County. However, in 1663, Northampton County was divided into two counties. The southern half remained Northampton County while the northern half once again became Accomac County -- later spelled Accomack.</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Northamptonshire" title="Northamptonshire">Northamptonshire</a>, England
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7004120040000000000♠">12,004</span>
</td>
<td><span data-sort-value="7002207000000000000♠">207</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7002536000000000000♠">536</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
