<td><span data-sort-value="7002315000000000000♠">315</span>&#160;sq&#160;mi<br />(<span data-sort-value="7002816000000000000♠">816</span>&#160;km<sup>2</sup>)</td>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Nottoway_County.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="State map highlighting Nottoway County"><img alt="State map highlighting Nottoway County" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Nottoway_County.svg/250px-Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Nottoway_County.svg.png" decoding="async" width="150" height="65" class="mw-file-element" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Nottoway_County.svg/330px-Map_of_Virginia_highlighting_Nottoway_County.svg.png 2x" data-file-width="2495" data-file-height="1082" /></a></span>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="/wiki/Orange_County,_Virginia" title="Orange County, Virginia">Orange&#32;County</a>
</th>
<td><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.census.gov/quickfacts/table/PST045215/51137,00">137</a>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Orange,_Virginia" title="Orange, Virginia">Orange</a></td>
<td>1734</td>
<td>Settlers established the legal entity of Orange County in 1734 from a portion of <a href="/wiki/Spotsylvania_County,_Virginia" title="Spotsylvania County, Virginia">Spotsylvania County, Virginia</a>.</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/William_IV,_Prince_of_Orange" title="William IV, Prince of Orange">William IV, Prince of Orange</a>, to celebrate his marriage to the Royal Princess Anne of the House of Hanover, England on March 25, 1734.   The county was formed on August 8, 1734
